# Rust workspace build output (the native `gsa` engine)
/target

# Session memory layer: the ACTIVE buffer is a tracked stub so a clean
# checkout has the documented layout, while per-action exports and any other
# scratch (rule batches, journal batches, split simulations) are never
# committed. `git add -A` must not be able to commit an export.
.logs/*
!.logs/scratchpad.md

# Builder runtime state
.state/
.build-logs/
.pkg-cache/
.lane*.result
.pacman-install.lock

# makepkg outputs and downloaded sources
**/src/
# …but the Rust workspace's source trees are repo content, not makepkg state
!crates/*/src/
!crates/*/src/**
**/pkg/
**/build/
**/_build/
**/.git/
**/keys/
packages/*/*/*/
!packages/*/*/LICENSES/
!packages/*/*/LICENSES/**
*.pkg.tar.*
*.src.tar.*
*.tar
*.tar.*
# Upstream archive types "*.tar.*" does not reach. The engine derives its
# download set from THESE rules (`gsa-maint`'s `download_patterns`), so this
# block is both an ignore list and the maintain surface's classification: a new
# archive type needs its rule here, or `-M` will not treat a stray download as
# one. The recipe repository mirrors the same set in its own `.gitignore`, and
# its `tests/recipe-sources.sh` fails when a non-URL source=() entry exists on
# disk but is not committed — so a missing negation there is caught, not silent.
# When the two drifted before the split, a cleanup left ten downloads behind for
# a commit sweep to pick up (2026-09-20).
*.tgz
*.zip
*.jar
*.ttf
*.whl
*.part
*.sig
*.asc
*.log
*.log.*

# Host-specific profiles, generated configurations, and credentials
afdo.prof
propeller_cc_profile.txt
propeller_ld_profile.txt
config-[0-9]*
*.profraw
*.gcda
*.gcno
*.enc

# Temporary metadata and local reports
*.tmp.*
.srcinfo.err
